<UNDEF> UNDEF

Code-speak for undefined, or simply put - an error! If you see this pop
up, please BUG it for examination.

See Also: BUG
#
"ABILITY POINTS"

These points are a numerical representation of how much you can improve
your abilities. They are earned at a rate of 1 per level.

See Also: ABILITIES
#
AC ARMOR

"AC" is your armor class.

Items often have one of two effects: ac-apply, or "armor". These two are 
inverses of one another; ac-apply 10 = armor -10;
You can get a rough idea of what your current armor class is in SCORE.

See Also: SCORE
#
ACCOUNT ACCOUNTS

Each player has an account in which they can have a maximum of three
characters. The account is password protected so you must ensure its
security - if something "bad" happens to one or all of your characters
as a result of sharing your password, you will NOT be compensated.

See Also: PASSWORD
#
AFK

Usage: afk

AFK means "away from keyboard". Use this command when you're going afk to
get a beer, smoke a cigarette, etc. It simply lets people who TELL to you
know you are AFK and might not get the message. Type AFK again to toggle
it off.
#
AGE

Age is the game mechanic that measures how old your character is in
game terms.  Most characters start in their teens and gradually grow
older from there. Rumors abound throughout the land of a magical means
in which to decrease your age. You can see how old your character is in
SCORE.

See Also: SCORE

#
ALCHEMY

Alchemy is a necessary skill in the mixing or combination of a number
of ingredients to produce a product. A common example within Dark
Pawns is the mixing of reagents to produce a magical potion.

See Also: MIX INGREDIENTS

#
ALIGNMENT GOOD EVIL NEUTRAL

Alignment is the measure of how Good, Evil or Neutral you are, relative 
to the rest of the world.  In effects what kind of spells you can cast, 
what types of equipment you can wear, whether certain creatures act
aggressively towards you, etc.  You can see your relative current 
alignment in SCORE. It ranges from:

You are the Epitome of Righteousness!	(extremely good)
You're so good, you make the angels jealous.
You are feeling pretty righteous.
You are aligned with the path of right.
You are feeling pretty good today.
You are a little more good than neutral, but yet still bland.
You are neutral, how boring.		(completely neutral)
You are a little more evil than neutral, but not very exciting.
I actually think you would kill your own mother.
You are so evil it hurts.
Charles Manson is in your fan club.
You are the Epitome of Evil!		(the ultimate bad ass)

See Also: SCORE

#
APS

APS is the average-per-strike of damage done by a weapon. Since a weapon
can have a range of damage, you can expect to do an APS of damage points
each strike.

See Also: "DAMAGE DICE"
#
AREAS

Yep, there are some, go find 'em. The world is designed to be contiguous;
each zone buffing up against another in a logical way. The best way to find 
new areas is to ask other players, or just go out into the world and explore 
some.  Make sure you are adequately prepared first though.

#
ATTITUDE ATTITUDES 24 ATTI

As you progress in level, certain high-level mobs start paying a lot more
attention to you, in a bad way. Essentially, they "cop an attitude" and attack
you. Avoid them, kill them, or be killed.
#
BOARDS

Bulletin boards are the forum of inter-player communication on the MUD.
There are different bulletin boards for different purposes -- for example,
a standard mortal board, a board for immortals, a board for fun "social"
messages, etc.  Naturally, not all players may be allowed to read all
types of boards.

Type "LOOK BOARD" to see the messages already posted on a board.  Type
"WRITE <subject>" to post a message to a board; terminate a message with
a '@' as the first character on a line.  Type "READ <number>" to read a
post.  Type "REMOVE <number>" to remove your own messages.

Example:

  > look at board
  > write Am I using these boards correctly?
  [writes the message; terminates with a '@']
  > look at board
  > read 6
  > remove 6

See Also: MAIL READ WRITE
#
BRIBE HIRE

Mercenaries can be hired, the current market rate is variable depending on
your level.

Guards can be bribed; the price varies from guard to guard, but they 
don't come cheap.

To bribe or hire someone, just GIVE <amount> coins <person>

Examples:
> give 101 coins mercenary
> give 200 coins guard
#
BROADCAST BROADCASTS NOBROAD

The Broadcast channel displays arena fights live as they happen
to the whole world.  To turn on/off Broadcast, type TOGGLE BROAD.

See Also: TOGGLE
#
BROKEN

Should you be killed in combat, there is a chance that your items could be
broken. Broken items cannot be used or sold, but they can be repaired.

See Also: CRAFT REPAIR
#
CAMP CAMPING

A generic term used to indicate that a player, or group of players,
is remaining in the one location for an extended period of time. In
essence, this could mean continually killing the creatures of a zone
or doing a quest so that others cannot.

While not strictly prohibited, it is definately a poor attitude and
if it continues, your actions will be bought to the attention of
the staff.
#
CAP

Every skill and spell group has a competency CAP attached to it. This
cap represents the maximum competency that can be attained by using
the skills/spells within that group (assuming they improve).

The competency cap is based on the skill/spell group level: at level 1,
the cap is 25%; at level 2, the cap is 50%; at level 3, the cap is 75%;
and at level 4, the cap is 100%.

For example, the 'gate' spell within the 'Astral' spell group is level
2. Using the 'gate' spell successfully may improve your competency for the
'Astral' group, up until the point the group has a 50% competency. After
that, regardless of how often you successfully use the 'gate' spell, your
competency will not increase.
#
CASTLE CASTLES

On Dark Pawns, castles are a generic term for structures owned
and maintained by clans of players.  They can be anything from
small fortresses to hidden mountain strongholds to a secret 
back room at the local pub!  

After a clan has gained sufficent strength and noteriety in the
land, they may petition the staff for a castle.  Please note 
that there are no castles available for individuals, or groups of 
individuals who are not in a clan.

&cWhat it all costs:&n

Carving your own permenant niche in Dark Pawns is not easy. The 
following list is a break down of castle features, and their cost.
Note that some features may also require a quest to be performed,
and that only the basic features have been listed.

&cLand:&n

An initial investment of 100,000 gold coins buys you the basic
set up, which is 3 rooms, an entrance, foyer, and main room.
Additional rooms are 75,000 each.

Castle locations will be chosen by the gods, though your preferences 
will be taken into consideration.

&cFacilities:&n

Lockable doors, grates, portculli, etc. are available for an installation
charge of 15k.  They come with one key.  Additional keys are 10k.  Those
of you looking for greater security should consider installing a reinforced
door, which is 30k and comes with one key.

Statues and Fountains are 10k each.

Banking facilties are 20k.

Informational boards are 15k.

Local priests can be called in to bless certain chambers in your castle
for 80k per chamber.


&cCastle Staff:&n

Butlers, maids, slave girls, guards etc, are 1k per level, with a 
10k minimum each.  Please note that the staff of Dark Pawns cannot
take responsibilty for your failure to adequately defend your property.

&cAdditional Issues:&n

Over time, there will be associated upkeep costs that go in to maintaining
your property.  These costs will be deducted directly from your clan bank
account.

&cExample Castle and prices:&n

Initial Land:			       100,000
Reinforced Door (w/ 1 key)		30,000
2 extra keys				20,000
2 level 30 guards			60,000
1 Butler				10,000 (min)
1 Fountain				10,000
-----------------------------------------------
Grand Total:			       230,000


#
CHANGE CHANGES

Too many things have changed on Dark Pawns 2.2 for them to be listed here.
When in doubt, try the help files. If you still can't find what you are
looking for, typo it and we'll add it to help asap.
#
CITIZENSHIP

You can buy citizenship in several cities in Dark Pawns for a small fee.
Citizenship allows you to purchase a store within that city - you can
only be a citizen of one city at a time.

The "safe rooms" in the cities are generally the Temples or common 
Meeting places of the city.

See Also: HOMETOWNS STORE
#
CHARISMA WISDOM INTELLIGENCE STRENGTH DEXTERITY CONSTITUTION STATISTICS STATS

Statistics affect more facets of the game than can be listed.
Here's a short run-down of some of what they affect, and definitions.

&cStrength:&n     Affects the amount of items you can carry, how hard you can
              hit, and the number of hit points you gain per level.

&cIntelligence:&n Affects the outcome of spell casting, and the number of mana
              points you gain per level. It will also help to determine the
              likelihood of a skill/spell group competency increasing.
&cWisdom:&n       Affects your interaction with some of DP's creatures, and the
              number of mana points you gain per level. It will also help to
              determine the likelihood of a skill/spell group competency
              increasing.
&cDexterity:&n    Affects how often you hit, get hit and your movement points.
&cConstitution:&n Affects the number of hit points you gain per level and the
              rate at which they regenerate. Should your constitution reach 0,
              your character will be unable to log on (ie. effectively
              deleted)
&cCharisma:&n     Affects how some creatures treat you (like shopkeepers), the
              number of followers you can have and generally your hit, mana
              and movement point gains.

Don't let your statistics get below 0 because bad things can happen.
You can see your current statistics with the ABILITIES command.

See Also: ABILITIES "STRENGTH SPELL"
#
CLASS CLASSES

Dark Pawns does not have a specific class system in which you choose the
type of character you want. Instead, the idea of a "class" has been
extended to be much more dynamic and user-determined. By learning
different skill and spell groups, and choosing which abilities you
want to focus on, you determine the type of character you will have and
the skills you can use.

See Also: LEARN
#
CLERK

The city clerk is the hub of administration for the local area. He or she is
capable of changing your citizenship, allocating shops, pardoning your racial
hatreds and should be your first point of contact when starting out.

With your letter of introduction, the clerk is capable of providing you
with some basic equipment to get you on your way. Note that the letter of
introduction can only be used by the character it was created for!

See Also: CITIZENSHIP SHOP "RACE HATE"
#
CODE CODING

The source code that runs Dark Pawns was originally based on CircleMUD
version 3.0 beta (pl11).  It has evolved considerably since then, largely
due to the efforts of the following people:

		dkarnes   Derek L. Karnes    Serapis
		stevet    Stephen Thompson   Orodreth
		rparet    R. E. Paret        Frontline
		mcooper	  Matt Cooper	     Doragar


#
COMBAT

Combat is the very essence of Dark Pawns, when it is just the player or
players against the mob in the field of battle.  To that end, most of
the SPELLS and SKILLS in the game are designed to aid you in combat in some
way.

Combat on Dark Pawns takes the form of standard rounds. During each round,
you have the opportunity to hit your opponent, and he or she has the
opportunity to hit you.

The time interval between your hits is defined as combat wait, and is a
value based on the weight of items you carry over a specific threshold, and
the type of weapon (or bare handed) that you wield. You may find that certain
creatures hit you more often to every one of your hits - this would indicate
that the mob has a lower combat wait than you do.

You will be unable to use a skill, spell or weapon during this combat wait
period. This means that if you are carrying a lot of items, and subsequently
have a large combat wait, your decision to FLEE may take some time before it
is executed!

Combat is the chief way to gain experience, levels, and equipment on Dark Pawns.

See Also: SKILLS SPELLS
#
COMPETENCY

Your competency is reflected in the LEARN command, and represents your
ability to use the skills and spells within a certain group. The higher
your competency, the higher the chance your skill/spell will be
successful when used.

You can increase your competency by using the skills/spells within the
group. However, there is a set group cap which limits how high your
competency can go - as an example, you can't KICK your way to a 100%
group competency when it's relatively low in the skill group.

Your intelligence and wisdom also have a bearing on whether your
competency will increase with time. If your intelligence and wisdom are
low, don't expect competency to increase very much! There is also a
fixed period of time after a skill or spell improves in which you
can't improve it further - this prevents people from spamming a skill
or spell to boost their competency.

See Also: CAP LEARN "SKILL GROUPS" "SPELL GROUPS"
#
CORPSE

A corpse is all that remains of a vanquished mob or player. Anything
that the mob or player was wearing and holding will remain on the corpse
until retrieved. After a certain period of time, a corpse will decay and
any equipment contained on it will sit on the ground.

Certain creatures within the realm will automatically loot items from
you when you die. Should you be missing items when you return to the
world, seek out the creature that killed you.

Note that for players, only the player themselves may retrieve items from
their own corpse - other players are prevented from doing so.

See Also: DEATH RETRIEVE LOOT
#
COVERED COVER GLOW GLOWING HUM HUMMING

If you see something in your EQUIPMENT list that has "covered" by it, it
means just that: you have another piece of equipment covering it. (ie. 
gloves cover rings on your fingers) People looking at you can't see items 
that are covered.

Humming and glowing equipment mean exactly what they say, too. The 
equipment hums (makes a vibrating noise) or glows with a faint light 
(not enough to see by, but enough to be seen in the dark).
#
CRAFT

The craft of an object is a measure of how well it was constructed. Should
you be killed in combat, there is a chance that the items you were wearing
are BROKEN and subsequently cannot be used.

Craft ranges from:
  Flawless
  Nearly Flawless
  Exqusitely crafted
  Finely crafted
  Well crafted
  Decently crafted
  Shabbily crafted
  Poorly crafted
  Broken

See Also: BROKEN REPAIR
#
DAMAGE "RACE HATE" "RACIAL HATRED" HATE HATRED

Damage done with weapons is determined by the weapon itself, as well as any
additional DAMROLL you posses. The higher your DAMROLL, the greater the
weapon damage will be. Word of your exploits will soon reach all over the
globe so if you continually kill creatures of a certain race, they will
adopt an aggressive stance towards you and generally attack you on sight
before you can get to them!

See Also: DAMROLL
#
"DAMAGE DICE"

Weapon damage is calculated by a "dice throw" which is completely transparent
to you. The first figure is the number of dice thrown, and the second figure
is the number of sides of the second dice.

For example, a sword with damage dice of 3D4 would indicate 3 dice are thrown,
each dice with 4 sides. This leads to a damage range of 0 to 12 points.

See Also: APR
#
"DARK PAWNS"

The very game you're playing now!
#
DIE DEATH CONDIE

When you die, you come back into the game in the temple or your last BIND
position. All equipment and gold remains in your corpse at the place you
died. To retrieve your objects, go back to where you died and get them from
your body. Alternatively, you could RETRIEVE your corpse from the Mortician. 

Every time you die, you will not lose any experience but you will gain 1
vitae point which reduces your character's abilities. If your constitution
ever drops below 1, you will be dead forever. There are places within the game
where vitae can be bought, rather than worked off in battle.

See Also: BIND CONSTITUTION VITAE RETRIEVE 
#
"DEATH TRAP" DT DEATHTRAP

A "death-trap" is a place in the world which upon entering you are instantly
slain, loosing all equipment.  You do not lose EXP for dying, however you
cannot RETRIEVE your corpse. Since hitting a death trap is considered one of
the worst fates that can befall a player character, there are no death traps
that are hidden or unmarked in Dark Pawns.

See Also: EXP DEATH RETRIEVE
#
DEED

A deed is an official document of ownership, in this case of one of the many
stores available for player purchase. They can be obtained (at a price!) from
the city clerk and USED in any Empty Store.

If you USE the deed after a store has been set up, the store will be closed
up and you can GIVE the deed back to the city clerk for a refund (minus a few
book keeping costs).

See Also: SHOP OWNER
#
DELETE

If you wish to delete your character, you may do so from the main menu,
which is displayed before entering the game.

#
DREAM DREAMS NIGHTMARE NIGHTMARES

When you sleep on Dark Pawns, there is a good chance that you might DREAM.
Most people in the world consider DREAMS to be harmless, but many mystics
and oracles consider dreams to be very important, even prophetic.  DREAMS
that occur in the Wyldlands are considered especially meaningful.

It is rumored that in the magick-rich Wyldlands DREAMS have the power
to physically effect the dreamer, in essence, the DREAMS become real.

Some DREAMS are known to be savage and twisted in nature.  These DREAMS
are normally referred to as NIGHTMARES, and like their counterpart DREAMS,
are more intense in the Wyldlands.  Many adventurers report that their 
NIGHTMARES are most intense after they have been recently reincarnated.

See Also: SLEEP
#
DRUNK INTOXICATION

The land of Dark Pawns has numerous taverns and inns from which you may
purchase various forms of alcohol. While every adventurer sometimes needs
a frosty mug of ale to unwind, be wary of consuming too much. Should you
become intoxicated, your actions and speech will be severly affected and
pity the fool who enters into combat!
#
DYE DYES

Dyes have many uses, but the one of primary interest to you would be in
the design of tattoos. You will need to find a number of ingredients
and combine them to create a dye.

See Also: ALCHEMY TATTOO
#
ENCUMBRANCE WEIGHT ENCUMBERANCE PTS

Encumbrance is a three-dimensional assessment of mass, weight, and 
occupied space. Basically it's an assessment of how difficult something
is to carry around. i.e. 2-foot lead pole and a 10-foot wooden pole have
about the same encumbrance; the lead due mostly to weight; the wooden due
mostly to the awkward length.

Encumbrance affects spell casting, and is measured in "points" for lack
of a better unit. 
#
UNASSIGNED EXPERIENCE XP

Whenever you kill a monster, you earn experience points.  When enough 
experience points are earned, you raise a level.

Things you should know about experience points:
  * When in a group, the total experience is divided up amongst the
    group members, dependant on each member's level.

  * Dieing or fleeing from a battle does not decrease your experience points.

  * Killing a creature 10 or more levels below your own will give you no
    experience!

Your character also possesses unassigned experience, which increases at the
same rate as your experience. Unassigned experience is used to improve your
character, such as learning a new skill or improving an ability.

See Also: GROUP SCORE LEARN ABILITIES
#
EXHAUSTION EXHAUSTED TIRED FATIGUE

Your character will expend movement points when travelling - should these
reach 0, you will be unable to move further until they regenerate. You
will also need to sleep, or you will suffer from physical exhaustion and
be unable to carry out basic functions.

See Also: MOVEMENT SLEEP
#
FAQ

Be sure to read the board in your local Temple. It contains messages
from other players and staff members on virtually any topic.

You also are going to want to read HELP POLICY (for the rules)
and HELP NEWBIE (for any "newbish" questions). Don't be afraid to
ask others for assistance, but don't expect everything to be
handed to you - you will need to show an ability to get along by
yourself in order to work well in a group.

******FAQ:(and the help files to read to find the answers)******
(Words in CAPITALS means type HELP <word-in-capitals> to see the
 help file)

&cWhere do I start?&n
  Your character will begin life in one of several larger cities. If you
  are new to the game, you should spend some time in the city getting
  familiar with the commands and game interaction.
&cWhere can I go to get experience?&n
  Larger cities, those with guards, do not look kindly upon their citizens
  being slaughtered. As such, you'll need to explore beyond the city walls
  to find creatures to kill - make use of the CONSIDER command.
&cI've got nothing, I'm broke, hungry and thirsty!&n
  You can CARVE food from your kills, and every city will have a source of
  food (although you'll need to pay for it) and water. You should save your
  gold to purchase better equipment from the stores within the city, or
  make usual trips to the city donation room to pick up items that have
  been left by others.
&cHow can I find out what skills/spells I know?&n
  LEARN. You will need to track down a TEACHER in order to acquire more
  skills and spells, and will need EXPERIENCE to learn them.
&cI didn't get a choice of class, what am I?&n
  Dark Pawns does not have a distinct class system. The type of character
  you wish to be should determine what skills and spells to learn - for
  those that like the art of magic, you should seek TEACHERs who train
  in spell groups as an example.
&cIs there a way to automate things, such as looting corpses and gold?&n
  AUTO
&cHELP!! I'm lost!!&n
  Typing RECALL will return you to the temple of your home city, unless
  you BIND yourself to another location. This, however, will only work
  while you are at a lower level - as your level progresses, you will
  need to purchase recall scrolls.

See Also: HELP
#
FLAGS DEAF WRITING MAILING

Players sometimes have FLAGS after their names in the WHO list.  These
flags are always in parentheses, not brackets or braces.

  FLAG        MEANING
  ----------- ---------------------------------------------------------
  (CHOSEN)    Player is the Chosen of the Gods.
  (invis)     Player is invisible; you can see him/her because you are
              sensitive to the presence of invisible things.
  (writing)   Player is writing on the board; do not disturb.
  (mailing)   Player is writing mail; do not disturb.
  (deaf)      Player has chosen not to hear shouts.
  (notell)    Player has chosen not to accept tells.
  (quest)     Player is participating in a quest currently being run by
              the gods.
  (AFK)       Player may be Away From the Keyboard and may not hear 
              anything.
  (OUTLAW)    Player is an OUTLAW.

See Also: NOSHOUT NOTELL QUEST STEAL VISIBLE OUTLAW
#
FOOD

As with all living creatures, your body will need food to function.
Food within Dark Pawns comes from a variety of places, generally it
can be purchased in one of the many shops within the realm. Failure
to eat (and drink) will leave your character hungry (and thirsty).

Food will degrade over time, to the point at which it will decay
completely and you will be left with nothing.

See Also: HUNGER THIRST
#
FORGE FORGER

There are creatures within the realm who can forge weaponry and armor
for your use, given the right tools and gold! Typing LIST in their
presence will indicate what items can be created for you. Typing
BUY <item> will have the item created and an amount of gold deducted.
#
GOD GODS

The Gods of Dark Pawns are a mysterious lot, preferring to remain 
obfuscated and mysterious to the mortal population.  It is known that 
they do speak to some mortals, however.

See Also: WIZLIST IMMLIST 
#
"GROUP POINTS"

In order to learn new spell and skill groups, you need to earn GROUP
POINTS which will occur at every 10 levels. These can be viewed under
your SCORE.

See Also: SCORE LEARN "SKILL GROUPS" "SPELL GROUPS"
#
HOMETOWN HOMETOWNS

Your hometown is the city that you have residence in.  Being a citizen in
your hometown entitles you to quit there for free.  Anyone can quit for 
free in the Temple in the free city of Kir Drax'in.  Other hometowns may
require you to pay a fee to become a citizen there.

Your hometown is displayed in the SCORE listing. When you recall, you 
will recall to your hometown. If you quit out in your hometown, you will
start there, if you quit out someplace else (like in Kir Drax'in) you 
will start there.

See Also: RECALL "WORD OF RECALL"
#
HITROLL HR DAMROLL DR "SAVING SPELL" "SAVING THROW" THROW SAVING DODGEROLL

Hitroll, Damroll, Dodgeroll and Saving Throws are some of the raw mechanics
of Dark Pawns.  Combat consists of two main elements: the chance to hit, and
the amount of damage done if a hit is successful. A few brief definitions:

Hitroll:   A bonus chance of hitting someone during combat. This bonus is
           applied to the attacker during a combat round.

Dodgeroll: A bonus chance of avoiding a hit during combat. This bonus is
           applied to the defender during a combat round.

Damroll:   The amount of damage you do, in addition to the average per round
           damage of your weapon.

Saving Throws: How well your character is protected against certain
               specialized attacks. A negative saving throw indicates better
               protection for that attack.

See Also: COMBAT                     
#
HUNGER THIRST HUNGRY THIRSTY

Your character will need a constant supply of food and beverages if
they are to survive. While not essential to play the game, hunger and
thirst will reduce your character's ability to regenerate hit points,
mana and movement. Things to eat and drink can be purchased from all
of the major cities.

See Also: EAT FOOD CARVE
#
IDENTIFY IDENTIFIER

Most cities will have an identifier, a creature who will identify all types
of equipment for a price. The result of the identification will depend on
the type of equipment being identified. Some of the more common flags
attached to items are described below:

NOBITS     - There is nothing special about this item
RNDLD_ZONE - The item randomly loads within a zone, so it may not appear in
             the same place twice
!RENT      - The item will not be saved with your character when you quit
ENCHANT    - The item has been enchanted
!PERSIST   - The item will not be saved during a mud reboot
BROKEN     - The item is useless unless it can be repaired
#
INGREDIENTS

Certain items within the Dark Pawns world will require ingredients in order
for you to be able to make them. An example would be collecting reagents to
make a specific potion, or plant life to make colored dyes.

See Also: ALCHEMY MIX POTION
#
IMPLEMENTOR

The most powerful being in existence.

See Also: IMMLIST WIZLIST
#
INN INNS CRYOGENIC CRYO RECEPTION

There is no rent on Dark Pawns, so you can quit at any point in the world
and have your items saved. However, should you be unable to log onto the
mud within a defined time frame, see HELP RENT, your items will be deleted
automatically.

To prevent this, a staff member can assign a CRYO flag to your character
which protects your rent file. This is not given out lightly and you will
need to explain your requirement for the flag.

See Also: RENT HOMETOWN QUIT REALLYQUIT
#
JAIL GUARDS GUARD CITYGUARD

City Law states that no violence is allowed within the confines of the city.
Offenders are thrown in jail for a short period of time which increases as
your level increases. Be warned that cityguards are given leeway to kill
offenders in protection of their own lives, and of course are always to rid
the city of WEREWOLVES and VAMPIRES.

See Also: BRIBE WEREWOLF VAMPIRE
#
LINK LINKLESS

A lot of players have problems with their links to the game.  This can be
very hazardous to your health in the middle of a battle, of course.

 I. If your link is broken, you will automatically attempt to flee each
    time someone attempts to hit you.  If you manage to flee, then you
    will be saved by divine forces, and put in a safe place until you
    reconnect to the game.

II. If your link jams (freezes), you have a problem.  The only solution 
    We can give is that you break your link as quickly as possible.  By
    breaking the link you can hope that the above procedure is initiated.

    Do not try to get out of a fight by breaking link.  You will be not
    reimbursed for any experience or equipment if you purposefully
    cut your link.
#
LOOT LOOTED

Looting, or being looted, occurs when the items on a corpse are removed
for personal gain by another. Looting of player corpses by other players
is strictly prohibited, and harsh penalties will result for anyone found
doing so.

The creatures of the realm, however, are immune from such a thing and
may loot items from you upon your death. Since such an event represents
a huge loss, only the 3 most valuable items will be taken from you, the
remainder will be left on your corpse where it fell.
#
MAGICK MAGIC

Magick is defined as the energy field that surrounds the world, giving 
it existence.  Mortals skilled in the magickal arts are able to manipulate
this energy to their own benefit, either through sorcery, the violent magick
of wizards, or through prayers to an idol or deity spirit, as clerics and
avatars do.  The civilized world fears sorcery and sorcerers for their
destructive powers, but they have no problem with religious magicks.  Thus,
clerics and other religious powers dominate modern civilization's societal
government.
#
HITPOINT HP MANA MOVE MOVEMENT

These values represent your characters basic ability to function in the
world of DP.

Hit points relate to your character's health and well-being. The higher
the number, the more damage you can take in battle and the healthier you
are. When this value reaches 0 or below, your character has been killed.

Mana is used when casting spells.  You must have a certain amount of mana
in order to cast any particular spell.  If you do not have enough mana to
cast the spell you must rest until you gain enough points to cast.

Movement is used to travel anywhere within the realm. Travelling by your
own means (ie. not mounted on an animal) will reduce your movement points
based on the type of terrain you are travelling through. When your movement
points are insufficient for the terrain, you be unable to travel any
futher.

See Also: REST SLEEP SPELLS MAGICK
#
MAP

As there are several large cities within the Dark Pawns realm, it will be
up to you to map them for yourself!
#
MOB MOBILE NPC MOBS

Generic term for any Non-Playing Character in the game.. i.e. "monsters".
#
MOONGATE MOON

There exists an extraordinary cosmic association between the gravity of 
the moon and the delicate fabric of time and space. As though pulling the
strings of some cosmic marionette, the moons cause radiant moongates to 
appear on the land below. Step through one of these shimmering corridors 
of light and you will be transported to a new time or place. Moongates 
generally appear at locations where fragments of extraterrestrial rocks 
called 'moonstones' have been buried. There are at least two types of 
moongates -- blue and red.

Blue moongates, generated by moonstones, generally focus on the 
destinations in but a single world -- the world in which they appear.

Red moongates, generated by the powerful Magi of the land, are summoned
by magicks, and thus can be opened at any time, even during the day.

See Also: TIME ENTER GATE
#
MULTI MULTIPLAYER

You are limited to playing with 3 characters (refer to the POLICY) on
Dark Pawns, although you can only have one character online at any one
time.

You should create characters with different skill and spell groupings,
so that they can be used in differing situations - be it as a healer,
or a fighter, or perhaps someone who masters in the art of stealth.
#
MUSHROOM

Magic mushrooms are created with the "create food" spell. The mushroom
given to new players at the start of the game is edible and not 
poisonous.
#
NAME NAMES

Character names MUST be fantasy oriented! If it is not, you run the risk
of being deleted without reimbursement (an obvious example would be
"Johnny" or "Timmy").

If the staff feel your name is not fantasy oriented, but is not totally
inappropriate, you will be asked to justify why you should keep it.
#
NEWBIE

The term "Newbie" is mud slang for "Junior to the game", usually a character
of low level or low experience. Use this time to learn the game, its commands
and some basic mudding techniques (such as killing mobs to obtain eq, and then
selling that eq for money).

Refer to the Dark Pawns website for the FAQ and use the HELP command often.

See Also: HELP
#
NOBITS

The term "NOBITS" is mud slang for "Has no bits". What it means, 
essentially, is that the item has no special affects to it. It
doesn't do anything remarkable.

#
OUTLAW OUTLAWS

All characters are created with the expectation that they will follow
the social rules of any civilised world. However, you have the option
of becoming an OUTLAW if you so wish, giving you ability to kill and
steal from your fellow OUTLAWs (you will be unable to use your new
found abilities on other players within Dark Pawns unless they have also
chosen to become an outlaw).

The choice to become an OUTLAW should not be made lightly, for you will
be unable to return to non-outlaw status until a certain period of time
has elapsed. Should you kill or steal from others, this time period will
be extended automatically.

Outlaws are generally not well liked and are known to be hunted and shunned
by many. City guards are especially not fond of such people and will
confine them to jail upon sight.

See Also: PK PSTEAL
#
OWNER STORES

Each major city is capable of supporting a number of player-owned stores,
the number varying depending on the city size. Apart from the initial purchase
cost, you will be responsible for monthly city taxes, staff wages (after
all, you need someone to run the shop for you!) and 50000 gold coins to give
to your shop keeper - no gold, no store!

You have a choice on the type of store and the goods the store accepts will
be based on this choice. You will be responsible for stocking the store with
an initial amount of goods and also ensuring the store keeper has a sufficient
amount of gold (both for purchasing goods from other players and paying the
monthly tax).

You will be warned if your store's gold drops below 20000 coins, and the store
will be liquidated if it runs out of gold. (The goods within the store will
also be sold off and the money put into the city coffers!)

Simply visit the city's clerk to purchase a deed, locate an empty store and
you're on your way to making a fortune! To alter the shop variables, use the
SHOP command whilst in the store. You can set the following:

  Opens at:    The time the shop will open (there are 28 hours in the day)
  Closes at:   The time the shop will close
  Buy rate:    Multiplied by an item's price, this will be the cost to the
               purchaser. (Minus a small fee)
  Sell rate:   Multiplied by an item's price, this will be the amount of
               gold given to the seller. (Minus a small fee)
  Item limit:  A limit of the number of items a shopkeep will buy

See Also: DEED SHOP
#
PARCHMENT

There are two distinct forms of parchment within Dark Pawns - one is a common
variety that can be purchased in certain stores and can be written on to
leave notes for your fellow players; the other is a scrolled parchment, that
occassionally are carried by any number of creatures throughout the realm.

These scrolled parchments, if used correctly, allow you to learn the spell
that they provide. They should not be confused with scrolls, which are
magical items that can cast a spell on you, an object or someone else.

See Also: SPELLS SCROLLS
#
PARDON

You can request a PARDON from one of the staff members to have your outlaw
status revoked, but this will be used very infrequently given that you
chose to become an outlaw!

You can also buy a pardon from a city clerk, which will appease the first
five races you've managed to accrue a racial hatred for. Simply specify the
name of the hatred you wish to remove, or select ALL to have the first five
removed.

  > buy pardon ungulate
    This will remove the racial hatred towards the Ungulate race

  > buy pardon all
    This will remove the first five of your racial hatreds

See Also: CLERK "RACE HATE"
#
PASSWORD

Your password is your "key" to the game...without it, you will not be
able to access your account and subsequently your characters. You should
choose a password that is both easy to remember, and difficult for others
to guess. Ultimately, the security of your password is your responsibility.

If something "bad" happens to one or all of your characters as a result of
sharing your password, you will NOT be compensated. Be aware that auto-
complete triggers that enter your password for you fall under this category.
#
PET PETS

Pets are either ones you have purchased from a store, or creatures you have
successfully charmed to do your bidding. If you leave your pet unattended
for an extended period of time, they will wander off never to be seen
again.

See Also: CHARM
#
PK "PLAYER KILLING" PKILL PKILLING PKILLER

Player killing is allowed on Dark Pawns but, as in life, there can be
serious consequences to killing another intelligent being.

In order to kill other players, you must elect to become an OUTLAW.
Only OUTLAWs can hunt and kill other OUTLAWs. Werewolves and Vampires, 
given their undead nature, can be staked by any player without the need
for an OUTLAW flag.

See Also: PSTEAL OUTLAW
#
POTION

A potion is a magickal liquid that provides certain beneficial (or
detrimental)effects when drunk. Potions are most commonly created with
the alchemy skill but can be purchased in a store.

See Also: ALCHEMY MIX
#
PROFANITY SWEARING

Yes...most people do it...that doesn't mean you have to as well! The
occassional slip is fine, but use profanity as every second word and
you'll be MUTED for it.

Work on your vocabulary, come up with something that doesn't require it!
#
PSTEAL "PLAYER STEALING" PSTEALING

Stealing from other players is allowed on Dark Pawns.

In order to steal from other players, you must elect to become an
OUTLAW. Only OUTLAWs can steal from other OUTLAWs.

You may NEVER junk equipment that you have stolen from other characters.
Junking of stolen equipment represents an irreplacable loss to the
character whose item it was.  If you junk equipment you steal, you will
be removed from the game.

Stealing items from other players corpses is prohibited and in most cases,
you will phsyically be unable to do so.

See Also: PK OUTLAW
#
PUDDLE PUDDLES

Puddles are formations of liquid occurring from rain or other liquid 
collecting in one spot. They dry up and disappear after a short time,
or after their contents are consumed.
#
RACE RACES

Race is a purely social construct.  It's all in your head, man.

Kir- From the lowlands and plains of Aerth.  Of medium height and build,
the Kir are adept fishers, hunters, and stonemasons, having built most of
the great cities of the world.  The Kir are the most populous race of 
humanoids in the world.

Antali- From the harsh mountains of the north continent the majority of 
these tall, rugged people live out a semi-nomadic lifestyle hunting 
migratory prey across the vast frozen peaks and tundras of the North.
Antali have a great sense of adventure, however, and can be found almost
anywhere in the world.

Xixian- Making up the majority of the humanoid population of Xix, the
southern continent, the Xixian people are a short and lithe race who
excel at seafaring and craftwork.  The majority of Xixians live on or
near the shores of the southern continent, as the ocean plays a large
part in their day-to-day lives. 

Your race currently has no bearing on the game whatsoever.
#
REAGENT REAGENTS COMPONENTS COMPONENT

Reagents (or spell components) are used to cast (or enhance the casting)
of magickal spells. Some very powerful spells can only be perfected by 
obtaining the correct components.

The reagents necessary for spells can be found throughout the world, and 
documentation on their use is in various scattered spell books. Reagents 
for widely known spells can be found at Apothcaries in any major city.
#
REIMBURSE REIMBURSEMENT

If you lose your equipment as a result of a crash or other game
error, a god will most likely reimburse you.  To get a reimbursement,
simple put something along the lines of "needs to Talk to a God" in
your TITLE.

Creature positions and item locations are now saved regularly so that
in the event of a crash, your items will be where you left them. This
means that if you died in the wilderness and a crash occurs, you will
need to run out and retrieve them.

In extreme circumstances, items may not save and you will be given
a reimbursement provided you can prove the item was yours to begin
with. This often involves another player acting as a witness - note
that severe penalties will result from attempted cheating.

See Also: POLICY
#
REPAIR

Those items BROKEN in combat can be repaired by certain blacksmiths
throughout the world, namely those found in major cities. This service
will cost you gold and the repaired object will have one level of craft
lower than it did previously. (ie. items will eventually become unrepairable)

See Also: BROKEN CRAFT
#
REQUIRE REQUIREMENT REQUIREMENTS

Every player has the natural ability to wield a weapon, regardless of its
type. However, some of the more advanced weapons within the game have a
skill requirement attached - this skill requirement can be determined by
having the weapon identified.

In order to use these higher-skill weapons, you must learn the appropriate
levels of the associated skill/spell groups. Each level of the group
corresponds to a level of proficiency with weapons.

The WEAPONRY group allows a character to wield all weapons, except for
staves. These can only be wielded by those who study spell-casting groups.
The STEALTH group will allow a character to wield daggers.

For example, a weapon with the requirement of 2 in SWORD will require you to
learn at least level 2 of the WEAPONRY skill group in order to wield it. A
staff with the requirement of 3 in STAFF will require you to learn at least
level 3 in any of the spell-casting groups.

See Also: WEAPONRY STEALTH IDENTIFY WIELD
#
"ROLE PLAYING" RP ROLE

Role playing essentially involves acting out the part of the character you
have created in all facets of their life, be it the type of people they
group with, the skills and spells they learn, their speech, etc.

While role playing is encouraged, it is not compulsory. If you take role
playing too far, you can also expect consequences as in real life. As an
example, you may choose to be a solitary warrior who kills everyone he
meets - however, your fellow players and the local citizens won't take
kindly to this and you can expect to be shunned and perhaps even hunted
down and killed for your actions!
#
RULES

No one document can clearly and adequately cover all of the rules associated
with Dark Pawns. However, you should be very familiar with the policy which
lays out clear indiscretions and associated punishments. No excuse will be
accepted if a component of the policy has been violated.

See Also: POLICY
#
SCAVENGE

Certain creatures throughout the realm have been known to take items left
lieing on the ground. Should you carelessly leave these items behind, or
if you fail to retrieve your corpse before it can decay, there's a good
chance your equipment will end up scattered around the world.

See Also: CORPSE RETRIEVE
#
SHOP SHOPS

Shops are places where the adventurer may purchase equipment for his 
quests, and where he may sell his treasure if he should manage to survive
the perils with his life and sanity intact.  Many shops trade only in a
specific type of merchandise.  Thus, a baker may well refuse to buy your
armor, even if it is of high quality!

To some people, the prospect of obtaining the entire inventory of a shop
by murdering the keeper may appear tempting - but beware: The shopkeepers
are often rugged, capable men; roughened by years of trading and, indeed,
surviving in a world where the only safe prospect is death in the end.

Each major city will have several empty stores which a player may buy
and open as their own. It will then be up to the player to initially stock
and maintain the inventory for the store. A monthly tax is collected by
city officials but any profit is left to the player.  Typing SHOP in your
store will display a number of variables which you can set, or allow you
to retrieve gold from your shop keeper.

See Also: BUY SELL LIST VALUE OWNER
#
"SKILL GROUPS" "GROUP SKILLS"

The skills of Dark Pawns fall into four distinct categories. They are:
Stealth, Field Craft, Hand to Hand and Weaponry. Once you are familiar
with the skill group, and reach the required level of knowledge, you
will automatically be able to use the skills within it.

See Also: TEACHER LEARN
#
SOMEONE

When you see something like:

Someone gossips, 'Anyone want to group?'.

or

Someone says, 'Hey there!'.

This means that the person that is speaking is INVISIBLE to you, you 
cannot see them for whatever reason.

#
SPAM SPAMMING

Spam can be defined in numerous ways and there are many interpretations of it.
In relation to this game, spam can be classed as follows:
  * The repetition of an action or phrase (eg. gossiping "Hello" 20 times)
  * The manipulation of multiple objects as a result of an alias or trigger

While this second class is generally permitted, it does annoy your fellow
players and you may be asked to go somewhere quiet to complete it. If you
consistently spam, your ability to speak or move (depending on the situation)
may be removed.

If you witness spamming, ask the individual to stop. If they refuse or
continue, report the matter to a member of staff. Please log the event in
case a staff member is not present.

See Also: ALIAS TRIGGERS
#
SPAWN RESPAWN

In order to keep the gameflow progressing, areas within the realm will
respawn at certain time intervals. That is, the creatures within it will
be reborn, items will be restocked (within limits), and doors/chests will
be closed and locked - all as if no one had been there before!
#
SPELL SPELLS

Spells fall into several descriptive categories based on their effects.
Damage, duration and effectiveness depends on a number of factors, from
caster's level, to victim's saving throw. See help on the individual
spell names for more information.

The spells themselves must be learned from the written word, usually in
the form of old parchaments carried by any number of creatures within
the realm. Note that teachers cannot teach you the spells themselves,
you need to find the parchaments. You MUST have learned the spell group
prior to using the parchament, or it will be wasted.

You must be in possession of (and holding) a wand of some description in
order to cast a spell.

See Also: CAST MAGICK LEARN "SPELL GROUPS"
#
"SPELL GROUPS"

The spells of Dark Pawns fall into nine distinct categories. They are:
Rejuvenation, Protection, Malediction, Environmental, Astral, Detection,
Psychic, Necromancy and Utility. You must seek out teachers who can
impart the knowledge of these spell groups to you prior to physically
learning the spells themselves.

See Also: SPELLS TEACHER LEARN
#
TANK

The tank is defined as "the person being hit by the person you are 
fighting."

See Also: COMBAT
#
TATTOO TATTOOS

Tattoos are available from tattooists in most major cities, plus various
traveling magi knowledgeable of the art. Some tattoos give a bonus to
statistics, other give you spell effects. Tattoos are permanent until you
die, or are removed by a god (via a quest).

Due to the magickal nature of tattoos, only one tattoo can be worn at a 
time.

You will require a tattoo design and anywhere from one to three dyes in
order to get a tattoo. LIST will display available tattoos (based on
which designs you carry) and the cost for each. BUY <tattoo number> <colors>
will start the (rather painful) process.

Every tattoo design will apply a type of bonus, while each dye applies a
specific effect to the tattoo design, not all of which are beneficial!
Tattoo designs can be found scattered through the world in the form of
runes, while dyes are something you'll need to make for yourself.

See Also: ALCHEMY
#
TICK

A tick is a measure of time used by the game to keep things moving along,
such as the movement of the NPCs, the rising and setting of the suns,
the progress of weather, etc.

There are a few different ticks used in the game, but the two that would
interest a player are every 60 seconds, and every 4 minutes. 
#
TITAN

These beings have moved beyond mere immortality, and into godhood...

See Also: WIZLIST IMMLIST GODS
#
TOWN

The realm of Dark Pawns contains a number of towns which can provide any
number of services, from a weaponsmith to a stable for your horse. You may
only be a citizen of one town at a time.

See Also: CITIZENSHIP
#
TRIGGER TRIGGERS

A trigger is an automated response to a certain output from the mud. Triggers
are not a part of the mud itself and are dependant upon your mud client. Be
careful about the triggers you use - spamming will not be tolerated and
could ultimately result in the deletion of your character if it continues.
Refer to your mud client documentaton or speak to fellow players if you wish
to develop triggers.

See Also: SPAM
#
TWINK

Twink is a state of mind.

See Also: PAW
#
VAMPIRISM VAMPIRE VAMPIRES

Notorious for their sharp fangs and aversion to wooden STAKEs and garlic,
vampires are night creatures that live off of the blood of others.

Any race can become a vampire, either by certain dark incantations or 
(more commonly) the bite of another vampire.

Vampires can be killed just like any other creature (by depleting their 
hit-points) or by being staked. A wooden stake through the heart of a 
vampire is a sure-fire death, albeit a risky one... Vampires usually 
don't take kindly to failed attempts at staking them.  A successful
stake removes all vestiges of vampirism from the player when 
they re-enter the game.

Vampires can TRANSFORM at night to assume their vampiric form... gaining
a substantial amount (up to 2 times normal!) of mana points, based on the
phase of the moon. (New moon being the weakest gain, full moon being the largest.)
At dawn, the vampire can transform back to their normal shape.

While in vampire form, vampires can BITE a victim to drink their blood, 
or pass on their vampirism. Biting while fighting does damage, otherwise
it only causes damage if you fail to bite successfully. A vampire's 
hunger and thirst at night can only be sated by blood.

See Also: STAKE TRANSFORM BITE TIME

#
LYCANTHROPY WEREWOLF WEREWOLVES LYCANTHROPE

Werewolves (also known as lycanthropes) are part man and part wolf, known
for their excessive appetites and superior strength.

Werewolves are created by the darkest of magicks, or (more commonly) the
BITE of another werewolf. Lycanthropy is almost like a disease, spreading
through populations and transforming them entirely into werewolves who 
soon crowd themselves into extinction by devouring the available food 
supply -- and each other.

Lycanthropes can harness the power of the moon, TRANSFORMing at night to 
assume their werewolf form. Based on the phase of the moon, the werewolf
gains up to two times normal hitpoints (Quarter moon being the smallest 
gain, full moon being the largest.) Werewolves can not transform if there 
is no moon in the sky (i.e. in the new moon phase).

Although they can be killed like any other creature (by depleting their 
hitpoints), the quickest way to kill one is with a silver SPIKE through 
the chest. A successful spike removes all vestiges of lycanthropy from 
the player when they re-enter the game.

Werewolves have an increased metabolism (get hungry more often than normal
mortals) but can eat corpses, even though it's not a pretty sight.

Werewolves are forced to TRANSFORM during full moons.

See Also: SPIKE TRANSFORM BITE TIME
#
SKILLS

Your character can naturally do several things when first created, such as
wield a sword or fight hand-to-hand. Some of the more complex skills must
be taught and you should seek out one of the many teachers within the land
to train you and increase your abilities.

See Also: LEARN TEACHER
#
TEACHER TEACHERS

These are creatures within the realm who are willing to improve your
character's abilities. Their services are not free and they can be found
in any major city. Some of the more rare abilities can only be taught by
the best teachers, and these creatures tend to live in seclusion or roam
the land.

See Also: LEARN
#
VITAE

Your vitae is essentially your life force. Each time you die, you lose some
of that life force which is represented by vitae points - each vitae point
you accrue deducts from your character's overall ability. That is, you will
lose one point from each of your abilities. Vitae experience is the amount
of experience required in order to reduce your vitae point total.

Note: Your experience will continue to increase even though you may have
vitae points, but you will not be able to advance in level until all of
your vitae points have been cleared.

Should you die enough times in a short period of time, your vitae points
will increase to the point where your character will lose all ability and
subsequently may permanently die.

See Also: DEATH CONSTITUTION
#
WEAPON WEAPONS

Weapons in Dark Pawns have been sub-divided into 7 generic types: sword,
axe, staff, spear, mace, dagger and whip. These subtypes refer to the
weapon design (eg. a small, sharp blade will most likely be a dagger).

When you identify a weapon, you will be shown the damage dice and average
per round damage. Generally, the more expensive a weapon, the better these
statistics will be.

Note: Some of the magickal races you meet will be unharmed by conventional
weapons. You must find a weapon flagged as MAGIC in order to kill these
creatures.

See Also: "DAMAGE DICE" APR IDENTIFY
#
LEG LEGEND LEGENDS

These are gods that have contributed a lot to the world that is Dark Pawns.
They have decided, for whatever reason, to move onto new and better things.

Respect them, because the rest of the Pantheon does.
#
CIRCLEMUD 

                    C  I  R  C  L  E  M  U  D     3  .  0

